    ":question/id": "797519b5-ee4f-5bc0-bbbc-671debb4c9ad",
    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-130243",
    ":question/problem": "Calculate the product $A{I}_{2}$ given that ${I}_{2}$ is the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix and\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and ${I}_{2}$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n\n$$\nA\\cdot {I}_{2}=A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"
  },
