    ":question/problem": "Calculate the product $D{I}_{2}$ given that ${I}_{2}$ is the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix and\n$$\n\\displaystyle D=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$D\\cdot I_2=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>{{field-4}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix $D$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and ${I}_{2}$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n\n$$\nD\\cdot {I}_{2}=D=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"
